    "content": "All 19 checklist items have been tested and recorded.\n\n## Summary\n\n**17 PASS / 2 FAIL**\n\nCore task management is solid: creation with full detail retention, editing, deletion, completion with correct count updates, active/completed view switching, priority and deadline sorting (including undated-tasks-last), empty-title guard, and cycle prevention (both direct and transitive dependents are omitted from the prerequisite picker). The dependency visualization also works well — dashed SVG connectors and warning badges both open \"Dependency Chain\" tooltips listing each task's pending state.\n\n**Two defects found:**\n\n**FT-3 — Blocked tasks are completely uneditable.** The spec requires that a blocked task keep its description and priority editable while title and deadline are locked. Instead the edit button is outright `disabled`, and a DOM scan of the blocked card confirms only three controls exist (complete: disabled, edit: disabled, delete: enabled). There is no inline or alternative path to change description or priority, so the partial-edit behavior is entirely missing rather than partially implemented.\n\n**CS-22 — Reopening a prerequisite corrupts its completed dependent (most serious).** After completing \"Review project proposal\" and then its dependent \"Complete tax filing\", reopening the prerequisite was permitted with no warning and no cascade. \"Complete tax filing\" is now rendered in the completed view with `state=\"completed\"` and line-through styling *while simultaneously* showing `Prerequisite \"Review project proposal\" incomplete`. Critically, both its complete toggle and edit button are disabled in this state, so the user has no way to reopen or repair it — the task is permanently stranded in a contradictory completed-and-blocked state, recoverable only by deletion. This is worth prioritizing, since the invalid state is unreachable-from and unrecoverable through the UI."
